## Task 4 — Eight-direction requirements

The four-direction assumption is encoded in:

- [WizardAnimationController.cs](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/WizardAnimationController.cs:25): canonical initial direction is `south-east`; `DirectionFor` and `StableDirectionFor` return only the four diagonal names.
- [DoorPrototypeGlobalSceneBuilder.cs](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/World/DoorPrototypeGlobalSceneBuilder.cs:47): `WizardDirections` contains only four diagonals. The builder loops over this array to create clips and Animator states. Its standing-source array already contains all eight directions.
- [Generated wizard assets](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Art/Wizard/Generated): exactly 32 `.anim` files—eight per diagonal and none for cardinal directions.
- [WizardAnimator.controller](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Art/Wizard/Generated/WizardAnimator.controller): exactly 32 serialized diagonal states and clip bindings.
- [WizardArtIntegrationTests.cs](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/WizardArtIntegrationTests.cs:22): asserts 128 source sprites and 32 generated clips, plus the `south-east` initial state.
- [WizardAnimationPlayModeTests.cs](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/WizardAnimationPlayModeTests.cs:124): test vectors and expected directions cover only the four diagonals; other tests hard-code `south-east` initialization and diagonal state names.
- [NSC-070.yaml](/workspace/Tasks/NSC-070.yaml:40): explicitly fixes the inventory at 32 states/clips and four diagonals.
- [NSC-062.yaml](/workspace/Tasks/NSC-062.yaml:46) and [NSC-061.yaml](/workspace/Tasks/NSC-061.yaml:40): establish the earlier four-diagonal source and integration requirements.
- [PIXELLAB_GENERATION.md](/workspace/Docs/Art/Wizard/PIXELLAB_GENERATION.md:31) and `source-inventory.json`: document only diagonal walk directories as authorized gameplay animation.
- The builder, integration tests, Play Mode tests, and wizard-selection tests also repeat `south-east` as the canonical initial/preview direction. That default can remain valid in an eight-direction system.

The clips and controller are generated by `DoorPrototypeGlobalSceneBuilder.BuildWizardAnimationAssets()`:

- `EnsureWizardClip()` creates or updates `.anim` assets.
- `EnsureWizardState()` creates or rebinds Animator states.
- `AnimatorController.CreateAnimatorControllerAtPath()` creates the controller when absent.
- Sprite imports and curves are written through Unity editor APIs.

Yes, a menu command rebuilds them: [DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.Build](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:102), exposed as **No Safe Circle → Build Door Prototype Scene**, invokes the global builder as part of rebuilding and saving the scene.

An eight-direction implementation would require:

- Integrating the 96 cardinal PNGs and their `.meta` files.
- Replacing the dominant-axis four-way classifier with stable eight-sector classification and boundary hysteresis.
- Expanding generation from 32 to 64 clips/states.
- Rebuilding through Unity rather than editing serialization.
- Updating source-count, exact state/clip mapping, eight-direction Play Mode, lobby/input, and visual tests.
- Vincent visually testing all four wizards in all eight directions.

At minimum, NSC-070 requires revision because its 32-state requirement conflicts with eight-direction behavior. NSC-061 and NSC-062 also require revision if their original four-direction acceptance criteria are to become current eight-direction requirements. Notably, [NSC-074.yaml](/workspace/Tasks/NSC-074.yaml:1) already defines cardinal source acquisition, and [NSC-075.yaml](/workspace/Tasks/NSC-075.yaml:1) already describes the 64-state eight-direction integration. That existing contract relationship needs Vincent’s decision; I did not reconcile or modify it.

